
> A **transformer** is an electrical device that transfers electrical energy between two or more circuits through electromagnetic induction. Its primary function is to change the voltage level of an alternating current (AC) supply—either stepping it up (increasing voltage) or stepping it down (decreasing voltage)—while keeping the frequency constant.

